## Blocker found by the previous run (`doc/plan/c016-worklog/c-cross-language-e2e-summary.md`)
`cmake --build framework/languages/cpp/build/linux-ninja-c-e2e -j16` fails:
`samples/Bingo/Shared/Contracts/messages.hpp:4: #include "bingo_messages.pb.h": No such file or directory`.
`framework/languages/cpp/CMakeLists.txt:623-632` `add_zlink_protobuf_schema()` calls `protobuf_generate(
TARGET … IMPORT_DIRS "${proto_dir}" PROTOC_OUT_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}")` and adds only
`${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}` as a public include dir. On this machine (Ubuntu 24.04 system protobuf
3.21.12, found via `find_package(protobuf CONFIG)` or the `Protobuf` module — check which one won in
`CMakeCache.txt`) the generated header lands at
`build/linux-ninja-c-e2e/samples/Bingo/Shared/Contracts/bingo_messages.pb.h` (source-relative subdir
preserved), so the include path is wrong. With vcpkg's protobuf (the tree's original environment) it
lands at the build root. Both layouts must work.

